[ti:Day 04]

[00:00.00]victim 例 Many businesses have offered large amounts of financial aid or material relief to the victims of the earthquake. 许多企业已主动 向地震受害者提供了大量的经济援助或者物资救 助。
[00:14.81]precocious 例 Adolescents are among the most voracious and precocious users of mobile Internet services. 青少年是移动互联网使用者中最狂热、 最早熟的群体。
[00:27.73]culminate 例 He is the driving force on bilateral talks on trade, which should culminate in the next few months in a meeting of foreign ministers. 他在 贸易双边会谈中起着推动作用，这种作用将在几 个月后的两国外交部部长见面会上达到高潮。
[00:45.15]earnest 例 Earnest money is usually paid to bind a contract between the importer and exporter. 在订立合约时，进口商一般要向出口商支付定 金。
[00:56.48]affidavit 例 My father was asked to sign an affidavit of financial support. 我父亲应要求签署了经济担保 书。
[01:05.48]likelihood 例 After you choose a proper partner, the likelihood of your success will increase. 当你选 择了合适的合作伙伴，你就更有可能取得成功。
[01:16.95]holistic 例 The landowners at the Western ranch have been using holistic management to streamline costs and enhance profits. 西部的农场主一直在 以整体管理法削减成本、提高利润。
[01:32.20]finite 例 In a world of finite resources, we need to change how we work to make the best use of every resource we have. 在资源有限的世界里， 我们需要改变工作方式，最大限度地利用所拥有 的每种资源。
[01:45.85]boundary 例 Air pollution respects no boundaries and we must make common efforts to protect the environment. 空气污染没有边界，我们必须共同 努力保护环境。
[01:59.06]yardstick 例 With patents becoming a new yardstick for performance evaluation, an increasing number of Chinese scholars have filed a patent application. 随着专利成为新的成绩衡量标准，越 来越多的中国学者提交了专利申请。
[02:17.94]correspondent 例 The following details of the organisation and routine have come into the possession of your correspondent. 你们的通讯员拥有这个机构 以及其日常事务的如下详细资料。
[02:33.18]snobbish 例 He is snobbish about mobile phones. 他假 充对手机很在行。
[02:38.85]eminent 例 The eminent speaker will use case studies to show how design can make businesses more efficient and desirable. 这位杰出的演讲者 将运用案例分析来阐述设计如何能够提升企业的 效率和吸引力。
[02:53.51]relinquish 例 He was forced to relinquish his job. 他被迫 辞职了。
[02:59.46]frenzy 例 The country now is gripped by a frenzy of nationalism. 这个国家现在正笼罩在民族主义狂 热中。
[03:07.02]designate 例 With the increasing demand for wilderness recreation, they plan to designate 60 percent of the area suitable to develop wilderness entertainment. 随着野外娱乐需求的增加，他们 打算指定此区域的60%进行野外娱乐开发。
[03:26.62]keynote 例 The keynote of the meeting is innovation. 会议的主旨是创新。
[03:32.86]block 例 She had a block transaction on the Hong Kong stock Exchange. 她在香港证券交易所进行 了巨额证券交易。
[03:40.99]revive 例 As soon as the price picks up, enquiries will immediately revive. 一旦价格回升，询盘将立即 恢复活跃。
[03:50.00]unveil 例 Ford unveiled the latest trends the brand would bring to its Chinese clientele last Monday. 上周一，福特公司展示了其品牌将带给 中国客户的最新理念。
[04:02.19]expropriation 例 Land expropriation is quite common now when building shopping malls. 现在征用土地来 建大型商场很普遍。
[04:12.79]acceptability 例 It is usually the customer that ultimately determines the acceptability of the product. 通 常是由顾客来最终决定产品是否可接受。
[04:25.72]abject 例 The attempt to take over the company has finally turned out to be an abject failure. 收购 那家公司的尝试最终以惨败告终。
[04:36.75]embed 例 It's impossible to embed other programming language here. 这里不可以嵌套其 他编程语言。
[04:44.88]exhibitor 例 Exhibitors from all industries are invited to the hi-tech exhibition once a year. 每年都会邀 请各行各业的参展商前来参加高科技展示会。
[04:56.35]format 例 We will discuss the advantages of one format over the other. 我们将讨论这种格式优于 另一格式的地方。
[05:04.63]abuse 例 The position of General Manager is potentially open to abuse. 总经理这个职位存在 滥用职权的潜在可能。
[05:13.05]charter 例 Charter schools, an alternative to other public schools, are part of the public education system and are not allowed to charge tuition. 特许学校是除公立学校之外的一 种选择，隶属于公共教育系统，但不允许收取学 费。
[05:30.77]gearing 例 What makes the industry ripe for restructuring is its operational gearing. 使得基 金行业重组时机成熟的是它的经营配称。
[05:41.22]relatively 例 We have to make do with relatively small profit margins at the beginning. 刚开始，我们 不得不想办法应对利润相对较少的困境。
[05:51.68]claim 例 We have to put in a claim against you for all the losses sustained. 对于所遭受的一切损 失，我们不得不向你方提出索赔。
[06:00.39]amount 例 Taken together, the economies of the European Union countries amount to just under 24% of the global economy. 把欧盟经济 体放在一起计算，其总额还不到全球经济总量的 24%。
[06:14.76]glitch 例 I cannot work out the marketing schedule today because the computer program has a glitch. 由于电脑程序出了毛病，我今天无法完成 市场营销计划。
[06:26.67]depreciate 例 The financial crisis caused many overseas assets to depreciate against the yuan. 那场金 融危机导致很多海外资产对人民币贬值。
[06:38.29]trajectory 例 I can hardly believe the upward trajectory of commodity prices in recent years. 我几乎不 敢相信近年来商品价格的上涨轨迹。
[06:49.61]impeccable 例 As the representative of the company, her manners at the party were impeccable. 作为公 司的代表，她在晚会上的举止无可挑剔。
[07:00.94]exceptional 例 Exceptional cases should be handled differently. 特殊情况应特殊处理。
[07:08.92]cornerstone 例 Trade has been a cornerstone of our growth and global development. 贸易一直是我 们的经济增长和全球发展的基石。
[07:18.80]expand 例 Expanding the business is always on his mind. 他时刻盘算着要扩展自己的生意。
[07:25.33]cheque 例 You may cash in this cheque at all times and all places. 你可以随时随地把这张支票兑成 现金。
[07:32.88]prowl 例 The company remains on the prowl to make some recent big purchases. 该公司一直在等待 机会准备最近进行大笔采购。
[07:41.89]confidential 例 The employer has always worried about his employees' taking confidential information with them out the door. 那位雇主总担心雇员会 把机密信息带出公司。
[07:57.28]fragile 例 Though the global business conditions have been much improved, the local investors' confidence remains fragile. 尽管全球经济状况 已改善良多，当地投资者的信心依旧很脆弱。
[08:12.52]back 例 Due to the demand for these goods exceeding the supply, we were on a huge back order. 由于这些货物供不应求，我们拖欠了很多 订单。
[08:23.27]capacity 例 What really concerns me is that there should be so little willingness or capacity to do anything. 真正令我忧虑的是，眼下竟然没有 多少意愿和能力来做些什么。
[08:36.34]utilise 例 He expected to utilise China's capital and market advantage to drive the company's development. 他期望利用中国的资本和市场优势 来推动公司的发展。
[08:49.40]credible 例 The failure of the US to develop any credible path for fiscal tightening is also grossly irresponsible. 美国未能开拓出一条收紧 财政政策的可信道路，这也是非常不负责任的行 为。
[09:03.34]quell 例 These latest measures have done nothing to quell the public's suspicion about the increase of house prices. 新措施一点都没有减 轻公众对房价上涨的怀疑。
[09:17.43]misfortune 例 He has suffered a good deal of misfortune over the years. 多年来他遭受了很多不幸。
[09:25.85]retool 例 They were forced to retool their business strategy in light of global realities. 他们被迫根 据全球局势更改了商业策略。
[09:36.74]portion 例 He takes a portion of his salary each month for savings. 他每月都拿出一部分工资用于储蓄。
[09:44.58]consensual 例 Probably the most important attribute of a contract is the consensual relationship between two parties. 合同最重要的特征可能在 于合同双方的自愿关系。
[09:59.10]bumper 例 A redesigned bumper should also be in store. 一个重新设计的保险杠也应储备其中。
